  "nl_text": "The rschema_0221 database is used to store information about customers, suppliers, products, product purchases, and sales records. The database contains five tables: Customer, Supplier, Product, Product_Purchase, and Sales_Record.\nThe Customer table contains information about individual customers, including their address, customer ID, name, and phone number. The Supplier table contains information about individual suppliers, including their address, responsible person's name and phone number, supplier ID, and supplier name.\nThe Product table contains information about individual products, including product ID, product name, stock, supplier ID, and unit price. The Product_Purchase table contains information about product purchases, including product ID, purchase price, purchase quantity, purchase time, supplier ID, total purchase price, and primary key (supplier ID, product ID, purchase time).\nThe Sales_Record table contains information about sales records, including customer ID, product ID, sale price, sale quantity, sale time, total sale price, and primary key (product ID, customer ID, sale time).\nThe foreign keys in the Product_Purchase and Sales_Record tables reference the corresponding tables, ensuring referential integrity. The primary keys in the Product_Purchase and Sales_Record tables ensure entity integrity. The indexes in the Product_Purchase and Sales_Record tables optimize query performance.",
  "gold_question": "The retail and wholesale industry requires efficient management systems to replace manual processes, in order to support business growth and meet increasing management needs. An effective management system can help businesses better organize customer, supplier, product, and sales records, improve work efficiency, reduce human errors, enhance customer satisfaction, and optimize inventory management and financial accounting. A small-scale retail or wholesale management system can be used to manage customer information, supplier information, product information, and sales records.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0221.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0221\nCREATE TABLE `Customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Supplier` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `stock` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `Supplier` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Product_Purchase` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_purchase_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`, `product_id`, `purchase_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_purchase_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `Supplier` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `product_purchase_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `Product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Sales_Record` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `sale_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_sale_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`, `customer_id`, `sale_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `Customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `Product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
